# Signal Lab Stack Guardrails

- Keep the required stack: Next.js, shadcn/ui, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query, React Hook Form, NestJS, PostgreSQL, Prisma, Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Docker Compose.
- Do not replace required technologies with equivalents unless the user explicitly asks and the tradeoff is documented.
- Prefer the shortest path that preserves the evaluator journey: one command to start, one UI action to create signals, one place to inspect each signal.
- When local infrastructure is unavailable, keep the repository reproducible and explain the missing external prerequisite instead of hiding the gap.
